                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Okay, so I've seen the other reviews for this game, and honestly, I am wondering if we are even playing the same game. Because this game is bad. I really wanted it to be not bad, because Warfare Studios usually puts out fairly high quality RPG Maker ganes, But, this game, Is. BAD, \n\nI mean, it's playable, but that's about the only thing it's got going for it. \n\nComplaint the First: The battles. They are annoying and repetitive. Also boring as heck. I am no stranger to The Grind, but when you are trying to avoid or run away from more battles than you are fighting, that is a sign there is something wrong. It gets a bit better later in the game when you get a few more abilities, but battles are still for the most part devoid of any suspense or need for strategy. The monster designs are uninspired and I find myself dreading each random encounter. I did find myself getting into it during a couple of the boss battles, but that's it. At least random encounters are visible on screen, so it is easy to avoid them. Onscreen monsters outside of battle are always a nice touch, and something I like in games. It was also interesting how some of them moved at different speeds, I guess. Still doesn't make up for the terrible battles.\n\nComplaint the Second: Level Design\nEvery dungeon is literally the same dungeon - a straight line with occasional branches that lead to treasure. Even the general size and shape of the passageways are the same. The only difference is the tileset and the monsters you encounter. But it seriously just felt like I was playing the same level over and over. \n\nComplaint the Third: Writing\nIn an RPG, the most important thing is the story. I can forgive even the WORST gameplay if the story and writing is good, or if it has a sense of humor. You will find none of this here. Not only is the story about the most cliche \"Chosen One\" plot I have ever come across, it also boasts cardboard, inorganic dialogue that does not feel like real people are saying it. I cannot bring myself to give a crap about any of the characters or what happens next because of this clumsy, heavy handed attempt at writing a story. Now, even a terrible story would be forgivable if the game knew how to laugh at itself. But no. It takes itself SUPER SERIOUSLY the entire time, except for a couple \"jokes\", and I use that in the loosest sense, about how the main character's best friend is kind of an idiot. Note that aside from being impulsive in general, said best friend did nothing to proimpt those jokes so they just felt hackneyed and out of place. \n\nIn summary, this game is bad. And this is coming from someone who regularly writes reviews that find redeeming qualities in some of the worst-rated games. This is coming from someone who will generally play anything that isn't rendered completely unplayable by bugs.  I was going to wait until I finished this game so I could give it a fair chance, especially since it's so short, but here I am, only about 1/2 to 2/3 of the way through and I can't take it anymore.  After the first hour, it took at least half a bottle of wine just to keep playing because honestly I can only tolerate this stuff if I'm tipsy. \n\nI hate myself for wasting this much time on it, and I hate myself even more knowing that I'm probably going to push myself to finish the dang thing within the next week or so in the vain hopes that it may suddenly get interesting in the second half. And I hate myself the most that I'm probably going to get the dang sequel at some point in the hopes that the second will be better than the first, because hey, Warfare Studios wouldn't put out TWO flops in a row, would they? \n\nBut either way, this game is bad. I don't see how it only has positive reviews. This game isn't worth what it costs. This game isn't even worth the measly 40 megabytes it takes up on my hard drive. This is probably one of the top five worst games I've ever played.",
